<p>11.8. <strong>Non-Disparagement.</strong> During the Term of this Agreement and thereafter,both Parties agree that they shall not, and shall ensure that their respectiveemployees, consultants, officers and directors do not, directly or indirectly,make, publish, or communicate to any person or entity or in any public forum(including but not limited to social media, industry review sites, or publiccommentary) any defamatory or disparaging remarks, comments, orstatements concerning the other Party or its Affiliates or its business,products, services, or employees.</p>
<p>For purposes of this Section, a 'disparaging statement' is any communicationwhich would tend to lower the reputation of the other Party in the eyes of areasonable person or discourage third parties from conducting business withsuch Party. Notwithstanding the foregoing, nothing in this clause shallpreclude either Party from providing truthful testimony as required by law orlegal process, or from making confidential statements in the context of a good-faith dispute resolution process as outlined in clause 11.13 of this Agreement.</p>
<p>11.9. <strong>Relationship:</strong> The Parties are independent contractors. This Agreement does not create a partnership, franchise, joint venture, agency, fiduciary or employment relationship between the Parties.</p>
<p>11.10. <strong>Waiver:</strong> No failure or delay by either Party in exercising any right under the Agreement will constitute a waiver of that right.</p>
<p>11.11. <strong>Severability:</strong> If any provision of this Agreement is held by a court of competent jurisdiction to be contrary to law, the provision will be deemed null and void, and the remaining provisions of this Agreement will remain in effect.</p>
<p>11.12. <strong>Assignment:</strong> The Customer shall not assign any of its rights and obligations under the Agreement without the prior written consent of ClearTax. ClearTax may assign or novate any or all of its rights and obligations under the Agreement or any part thereof including but not limited to the right to payments, to any of its Affiliates and successors in order to exercise any of the rights or perform any of the obligations under the Agreement.</p>
<p>11.13. <strong>Governing Law and Jurisdiction:</strong> The Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India, without regard to conflict of law principles. The courts, tribunals, councils, forums and other dispute resolution bodies at New Delhi, India shall have the exclusive jurisdiction to adjudicate upon any or all disputes arising out of or in connection with the Agreement.</p>
<p>11.14. <strong>Notice:</strong> The Customer shall direct notices under the Agreement to the following address. Attn: Legal Department, Defmacro Software Private Limited (aka ClearTax), Corporate Office: 23, 24 AMR Tech Park, Block 1, First Floor, Hosur Main Road, Hongasandra, Bangalore, Karnataka, India PIN- 560068Email: <a href="mailto:legal@clear.in">legal@clear.in</a>, <a href="mailto:compliance@cleartax.in">compliance@cleartax.in</a>.</p>
<p>11.15. <strong>Survival: </strong>Unless otherwise provided for<strong>, </strong>Clause 1 (<em>Definitions</em>), Clause 4 (<em>Charges and Payment</em>), Clause 5 (<em>Proprietary Rights</em>), Clause 7 (<em>Representations, Warranties and Disclaimers</em>), Clause 8 (<em>Indemnification</em>), Clause 9 (<em>Limitation of Liability</em>), Clause 10 (<em>Term and Termination</em>) and 11 (<em>General Provisions</em>) shall survive termination or expiration of the Agreement.</p>
<h3>Annexure 1</h3>
<p>CCC Integration</p>
<p><strong>1. Purpose<br></strong><br>This Agreement outlines the terms and conditions under which ClearTax will provide integration services for connecting the Customer's ERP system with Clear Compliance Cloud using the Clear GL Stream Add-on.</p>
<p><strong>2. Scope of Work<br></strong><br>2.1 Inclusions</p>
<p>1. Installation and configuration of the Clear GL Stream Add-on in the Customer's ERP environment.</p>
<p>2. Automated data extraction from ERP, secure uploading to Clear Compliance Cloud, and data transformation for GST Sale Register, GST Purchase Register, General Ledger.</p>
<p>3. Documentation and one-time training sessions for the Customer's functional team.</p>
<p>4. Hypercare support for one month following integration.</p>
<p>2.2 Exclusions</p>
<p>1. Any customization or maintenance of the Customer's ERP system beyond what is necessary for the integration.</p>
<p>2. Configuration and maintenance at the infrastructure level, including network or firewall settings.</p>
<p>3. Real-time data synchronization</p>
<p>4. On-site support services.</p>
<p><strong>3. Customer Responsibilities<br></strong><br>1. Provide the necessary access to ERP systems, including remote access and VPN credentials.</p>
<p>2. Complete all prerequisites, including whitelisting API hostnames and enabling required network configurations.</p>
<p>3. Provide sample data for testing and data confirmation, along with confirmation of test results.</p>
<p>4. Appoint a project leader and provide a SWAT team for collaboration during the integration process.</p>
<p><strong>4. Project Stages and Timelines<br></strong><br>The integration project will follow a structured life cycle with the following stages and timelines:</p>
<p>4.1. Plan Stage</p>
<p>1. <strong>Pre-kick-off Meeting</strong>: ClearTax and the Customer will set up a kick-off meeting within three (3) days from the Integration Asset Start Date (as set out in the Order Form) to understand the Customer's IT environment, introduce key stakeholders, and discuss the integration development project.</p>
<p>2. <strong>Prerequisites Closure</strong>: The Customer shall provide access to ClearTax's information technology systems, including developer provisioning and establishing network connectivity, within twenty-one (21) days from the kick-off meeting. This stage ensures that all activities to start the project are completed.</p>
<p>3. <strong>Kick-off Meeting</strong>: Formally introduce the teams, share the project plan, and ensure that all prerequisites are completed. The kick-off meeting will set realistic expectations for baselines such as milestone schedules and project schedules.</p>
<p>4.2. Design Stage</p>
<p>1. <strong>Requirements Gathering</strong>: Update query configurations and initiate the data extraction process. Conduct workshops to clarify requirements.</p>
<p>4.3. Develop Stage</p>
<p>1. <strong>Development</strong>: Replicate base models, initiate development, and perform testing for specific changes and functionalities. ClearTax will implement the integration development as per the agreed integration development plan within thirty-five (35) days of completing the prerequisites.</p>
<p>2. <strong>Data Reconciliation</strong>: End-to-end testing from ERP to Clear and reconciliation. Integration development will be delivered to the Customer for data confirmation upon completion.</p>
<p>4.4 Test Stage</p>
<p>1. <strong>Data Confirmation</strong>: Validate the transformed data with the Customer and get sign-off on the go-live. The Customer shall complete the data confirmation within twenty-one (21) days and notify ClearTax of its acceptance or any issues.</p>
<p>4.5 Deploy Stage</p>
<p>1. <strong>Cutover Activities</strong>: Execute final tasks, validate transformation, and perform smoke tests for production environments. ClearTax will move the integration to the production environment within ten (10) days of receiving the data confirmation sign-off.</p>
<p>4.6 Close Stage</p>
<p>1. <strong>Hyper Care Support</strong>: Provide one month of post-go-live support to address any issues related to the integration within the initially agreed-upon scope.</p>
<p>2. <strong>Annual Maintenance Contract (AMC)</strong>: Not included in the standard integration package. All changes post-go-live will be handled as Change Requests.</p>
<p><strong>5. Timelines and Grace Period<br></strong><br>The Parties hereby agree that the integration process shall in no event exceed ninety (90) days including grace period. A maximum of thirty (30) days grace period may be allowed to both Parties for delays in meeting the deliverables provided herein.</p>
<p><strong>6. Acceptance Criteria<br></strong><br>1. The integration will be considered successful and accepted by the Customer when the following conditions are met:</p>
<p>(a) Seamless connectivity between ERP and Clear Compliance Cloud.</p>
<p>(b) Successful data transfer, transformation, and ingestion of sales and purchase documents.</p>
<p>(c) Completion of data confirmation with all issues resolved to the satisfaction of both Parties.</p>
<p>(d) Confirmation from the Customer within 14 calendar days of handing over for data completion.</p>
<p><strong>7. Change Management<br></strong><br>Any changes to the initially agreed-upon scope must be formally requested and approved by both Parties. Changes may affect project timelines and costs.</p>
<p>7.1 Enhancement of Scope of Services: Notwithstanding anything to the contrary, the Customer agrees that any request for integration development which is not stipulated in the Order Form shall be considered as a request for enhancement of the scope of Services and may be provided by ClearTax, at its sole and absolute discretion, and at such additional cost as notified by ClearTax.</p>
<p>7.2 Post-Delivery ChangesAny request for changes post-delivery of the integration development must be in writing and shall set out in sufficient detail that the change requested is within the scope of Services set out in the Order Form and is in accordance with the agreed integration development plan. ClearTax shall then use commercially reasonable efforts to perform the changes requested to the extent feasible in ClearTax’s sole discretion and reissue the integration development to the Customer.</p>
<p>7.3 Additional Costs for Changes Post-Acceptance: The Customer shall be liable to make the entire payment as per the Integration Asset Start Date as set out in the Order Form. Any changes subsequent to acceptance of the integration development requested by the Customer, or if the scope of Services is not completed within the relevant time period set out above (including the grace period), may be carried out at the request of the Customer by ClearTax at its sole and absolute discretion, and at such additional cost as may be notified by ClearTax.</p>
<p><strong>8. No Refund or Waiver of Payment Obligations <br></strong><br>Notwithstanding anything contained in this Agreement, under no circumstance shall the Customer claim for a refund of any charges (including one-time charges under the Order Form) or seek a waiver of its payment obligations on account of the Customer’s delay (whether due to inactivity or otherwise) or failure to undertake the following within the relevant timelines set out above (including the grace period):</p>
<p>1. Providing access to its information technology systems, including developer provisioning and establishing network connectivity, past data for reconciliation, or failure to confirm and finalize all other requirements, if any, as may be required by ClearTax for integration development;</p>
<p>2. Verifying data and confirming acceptance of the integration development post handing over for data confirmation;</p>
<p>3. Notifying ClearTax of the issues or bugs in the integration development.</p>
